<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">What is AI-native search?</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">AI-native search</strong> is a search paradigm that understands natural language queries instead of matching keywords. When a user types "मलाई laptop को warranty बारेमा जानकारी चाहिन्छ" (I need information about laptop warranty), AI-native search understands the intent and returns the warranty policy directly&mdash;not a list of pages containing "laptop" and "warranty."
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    For Nepal, this matters because users naturally mix Nepali and English (code-switching), and traditional keyword search fails completely with these queries. AI-native search handles "best mobile phone 20,000 samma" as naturally as it handles pure English queries.
  </p>
</div>

